WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:08.580
I don't think Putin targeted Hillary

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.800
Clinton specifically; certainly not in

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.590
the outset of the elections. The idea was

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:16.410
to undermine the trust in the very

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:19.470
institution of US election, whether it's

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:21.090
on the Republican side or Democratic

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.730
side or local side or federal side. That

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.920
did not start with the US elections. It

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:27.990
happened with Russia's involvement all

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.000
over Western Europe and Eastern Europe.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.170
But as things progressed and it became

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:37.410
clear that Hillary Clinton was

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:38.850
going to be the nominee of the

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:41.460
Democratic Party, and especially since

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.129
she became the leading candidate, it was

00:00:44.129 --> 00:00:47.489
particularly sweet for Putin to attack

00:00:47.489 --> 00:00:50.879
her because there is bad blood between

00:00:50.879 --> 00:00:55.079
them. In 2011, when mass anti-Putin

00:00:55.079 --> 00:00:57.270
demonstrations swept throughout Russia,

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.550
he blamed the State Department for

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:02.489
organizing and paying for those

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:04.710
demonstrations and Hillary Clinton was

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.180
Secretary of State at the time.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:09.150
So what do you think about Russian

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:11.369
involvement in the US presidential election?

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:13.680
Let us know in the comments section, and

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:16.409
also let us know what other topics you

00:01:16.409 --> 00:01:19.000
want AEI scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

